From 54c806b11df43793d443878b407d5c866a6d3e61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] ARM: dts: gts28ltexx: SS333 modem node and SPI4 boot
 link

New exynos5433-gts28ltexx-modem-ss333.dtsi for sec_modem_v1:

- mif_pdata (root node, name kept for the cbd cp_status path): the ten
  control GPIOs as <name>-gpios, all GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH (the stock 0x1/0xf
  third cells would invert CP_ON/CP_RESET under gpiod), cp-status shared
  by mif,gpio_cp_status and link_pm/gpio_cp2ap_status, the samsung,mipi-lli
  and samsung,boot-spi probe phandles, the mif,* properties and the 13
  iodevs of the stock modem-ss333-pdata.dtsi (checked identical to the
  live device tree);
- no pin control on the CP lines, so they keep their reset/sboot state
  until allow_hw=1 (research/modem/research/review/kernel_boot_review.md
  E2, section 5.3);
- SPI4 @ 0x14d00000 enabled, bus pins gpv7-1/2/4 (function 3, pull-up),
  MISO gpv7-3 parked input pull-down, child spi_boot_link at 100 kHz.

Every value cites the stock dtsi and the live device tree line.  The
board includes this file from the merged series (section 18).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
